			"Message": "style(Air/Vine): Enforce formatting and PascalCase in gRPC server\n\nThis commit applies strict code formatting, variable naming normalization, and import updates to the `AirVinegRPCService` implementation, continuing the hygiene standards enforced across the Air codebase.\n\nKey changes include:\n- Updating import paths to reference the renamed `Vine::Generated::Air` module, aligning with the recent PascalCase module restructuring.\n- Converting local variables from `snake_case` to `PascalCase` (e.g., `connection_id` -> `ConnectionId`, `download_request_id` -> `DownloadRequestId`) within the service implementation and helper methods.\n- Removing redundant whitespace around type annotations (e.g., `Arc<ApplicationState>` instead of `Arc<ApplicationState>`).\n- Normalizing match arm expressions and async block formatting for structural consistency.\n\nThis ensures the `Air` daemon's primary gRPC service implementation adheres to the project's consistent style guide, reducing visual noise and maintaining architectural uniformity.",
			"SHA": "6311aa3719ea0f68af4316f694a6db27c9ea5752"
		},
