				55,
				1
			],
			"Message": "style(Air/Vine): Rename generated module to PascalCase convention\n\nThis commit updates the module declaration in `Source/Vine/Generated/mod.rs`, renaming the `air` module to `Air`. This aligns the module definition with the file naming of the generated `Air.rs` bindings and adheres to the strict PascalCase formatting standards currently being enforced across the `Air` element's codebase.\n\nThis change continues the codebase hygiene initiative seen in previous commits affecting the `Updates`, `Tracing`, and `Security` modules, ensuring uniform naming conventions throughout the `Air` daemon's implementation.",
			"SHA": "8710d60b30de1b842a8233efb621ac8b4bc09388"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-02-01T01:40:40Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				55,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Air/Vine): Add generated gRPC bindings for AirService\n\nThis commit introduces the `Source/Vine/Generated/Air.rs` file, auto-generated by `prost-build`, to establish the strongly-typed gRPC contract for the `Air` daemon.\n\nThe file provides the `tonic`-based `AirService` trait, client, and server boilerplate. It defines the complete Request/Response data transfer objects (DTOs) and RPC methods covering the `Air` daemon's capabilities:\n- **Authentication:** Provider login and token management.\n- **Updates:** Version checking, downloading, and patch application.\n- **Downloads:** Chunked file streaming with integrity verification.\n- **Indexing:** File system traversal and content search.\n- **Status & Monitoring:** Health checks, metrics, and resource usage telemetry.\n- **Configuration:** Dynamic runtime settings management.\n\nBy adding these generated bindings, the `Air` element now possesses the necessary type-safe IPC layer to implement the concrete logic for the `Vine` protocol.",
			"SHA": "aee6f94bbae9c4d7a87569103bffeb9dfd168e74"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-02-01T01:39:56Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				54,
				1
			],
			"Message": "style(Air): Enforce code formatting in Vine module\n\nThis commit applies strict code formatting and structural normalization to the `Source/Vine/Error.rs` file, continuing the hygiene standards enforced across the Air codebase in recent commits.\n\nSpecific adjustments include:\n- Normalizing indentation and removing redundant whitespace around type annotations (e.g., `err:tonic::transport::Error` instead of `err: tonic::transport::Error`).\n- Collapsing `From` trait implementations for `tonic`, `serde_json`, and `std` errors into single-line blocks for conciseness.\n- Ensuring consistent formatting across error variants and conversion logic.\n\nThis ensures the `Vine` module, responsible for defining error types for gRPC communication within the Land ecosystem, adheres to the project's consistent style guide, minimizing visual noise in future diffs.",
			"SHA": "2cc2f5cdc6e7c6b047653fa1d71cd527898bc2f8"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-02-01T01:39:31Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				54,
				1
			],
			"Message": "style(Air): Enforce code formatting in Updates module\n\nThis commit applies strict variable naming normalization and code cleanup to the `Source/Updates/mod.rs` file, continuing the hygiene standards enforced across the Air codebase in recent commits.\n\nSpecific adjustments include:\n- Converting local variables from `snake_case` to `PascalCase` (e.g., `platform_config` -> `PlatformConfig`, `status` -> `Status`) within the `UpdateManager` implementation.\n- Renaming circuit breaker interaction methods to match the PascalCase convention (e.g., `record_success()` -> `RecordSuccess()`, `record_failure()` -> `RecordFailure()`).\n- Refactoring the `format_size` utility method signature to accept `f64` instead of `u64` and updating call sites with explicit casting (`info.size as f64`).\n- Updating the `format_size` output format to include rate indicators (e.g., \"MB/s\").\n- Cleaning up long `while let` chains for better readability and prefixing unused variables with underscores (e.g., `device_id` -> `_device_id`).\n\nThis ensures the `Updates` module, responsible for version checking, downloading, and installation within the Air daemon, adheres to the project's consistent style guide, minimizing visual noise in future diffs.",
			"SHA": "2a722240b61d0a161204f9b20b0adc3bc4e51b6d"
		}
	],
